  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nOxford Open Doors: Christ Church Cathedral, Chapel of Remembrance Tour | 1030 – 12 September 2026\n£0.00\n\n20 available\nOxford Open Doors: Christ Church Cathedral, Chapel of Remembrance Tour | 1030 - 12 September 2026 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum will be running a tour of the Chapel of Remembrance, the regimental chapel for the county regiments, The Oxfordshire & Buckinghamshire Light Infantry and Oxfordshire Yeomanry.\n\nThe tour will last for around 30 minutes, starting at Cathedral porch. The tour will also cover the College War Memorials and other military memorials at the Cathedral and Cloister within the context of county, regimental history and remembrance.\n\nPlease meet for the tour at Tom Gate.\n\nThis tour is free, but please register your place as spaces are strictly limited.\n\n---\nPhoto Credit: Eleanor Sanger, Christ Church Cathedral\n\nDate: 12-September-2026\nTime: 10:30\n\nLocation: Christ Church, St Aldates, Oxford, OX1 1DP\nType: physical\n\nRelated products\nThe Origins of the Schlieffen Plan | Talk with Ross Beadle | 2pm Saturday 7 November 2026\n£12.00 Add to cart\nMeet Me at the Soldiers Museum | 2pm – 4pm | Thursday 4 June 2026\n£0.00 Add to cart\nMesopotamian Supper Club | IWAW | 6.30pm – 8.30pm Sun 21 June 2026\n£35.00 Add to cart\nFilm Screening: Theirs is the Glory (1946)\n£12.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
